DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -6, -6, -2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 2, 3, -10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 1, -8, 2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, -8, 2>") . Compute("<2, 3, -10>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<2, 3, -10>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<1, -8, 2>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, 3, -10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<2, 3, -10>") . Compute("<-6, -6, -2>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, 3, -10>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, -6, -2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<1, -8, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, -6, -2>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -3, -9, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -5, 10, -9 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -9, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -9, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -9, 2>") x Compute("<-5, 10, -9>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-3, -9, 2>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 10, -9>") . Compute("<-3, -9, 2>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, 10, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-5, 10, -9>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, 10, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-5, 10, -9>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, 0, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 1, -4, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, -4, -8>") . Compute("<3, 0, 0>")}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 0, 0>") x Compute("<1, -4, -8>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<1, -4, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<3, 0, 0>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<1, -4, -8>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, -4, -8>") x Compute("<3, 0, 0>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 0, 0>") . Compute("<1, -4, -8>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, 0, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 1, 1, 5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 0, 9, 10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<1, 1, 5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<0, 9, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<0, 9, 10>") x Compute("<1, 1, 5>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<0, 9, 10>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<1, 1, 5>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<1, 1, 5>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, 1, 5>") . Compute("<0, 9, 10>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<0, 9, 10>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -1, 4, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 5, 2, 7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-1, 4, -5>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<5, 2, 7>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 2, 7>") x Compute("<-1, 4, -5>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, 2, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 2, 7>") . Compute("<-1, 4, -5>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<5, 2, 7>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, 4, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-1, 4, -5>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 2, -4, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 6, -3, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 2, -8, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, -3, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<6, -3, -9>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, -4, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, -8, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, -4, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, -3, -9>") x Compute("<2, -8, -5>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<6, -3, -9>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<2, -4, -9>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, -3, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
